# No e-mail address in Maintainer, and that is deliberate rather than an
# omission. Debian convention puts one there and dpkg accepts the field without
# it. An address inside an artefact people download is a contact point and a
# correlation handle, published to everyone who installs -- and this
# repository's own anonymity sweep refuses one in a tracked file, which is how
# it was caught here before it shipped. Security reports go through the
# repository's private vulnerability reporting, which SECURITY.md names as the
# only channel that is both private and does not ask who you are.
Package: zycord
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Simstoshi
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/thesimstoshi/zycord
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6
Description: Zycord node and command-line tool
 A Zycord full node with the RandomX proof-of-work engine, so it joins mainnet
 and the public testnet, and zcd, the command-line tool for keys, wallets and
 protocol checks.
 .
 This package installs a systemd unit and does not enable it. A node needs a
 network and, to mine, a payout address, and starting one that has neither would
 be a service that runs and does nothing. See /etc/zycord/zycordd.conf.
 .
 These binaries are cgo builds and are not byte-identical across machines. The
 pure-Go tier is what a reader rebuilds and compares against SHA256SUMS.binaries;
 it is devnet-only and is not shipped, here or anywhere.
